{"availability":"available","full":"dmis-lab/Monet","name":"Monet","description":"[ICLR 2025] Monet: Mixture of Monosemantic Experts for Transformers","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":79,"forks":5,"created":"2024-12-06T04:43:04Z","updated":"2025-06-23T17:04:08Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.04139","topics":["iclr","iclr2025","interpretability","large-language-models","mixture-of-experts","sparse-autoencoders"],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/MonetLLM/monet-vd-1.4B-100BT-hf-viewer","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T13:01:44.003Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T13:01:44.003Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T13:01:44.003Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T04:52:28.912Z","stars":79,"forks":5},{"at":"2026-10-10T13:01:44.003Z","stars":79,"forks":5}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Monet presents a novel approach to enhancing mechanistic interpretability in large language models (LLMs) through an innovative Sparse Mixture-of-Experts (SMoE) architecture. By directly incorporating sparse dictionary learning into end-to-end pretraining, Monet addresses the fundamental challenge of polysemanticity - where individual neurons respond to multiple unrelated concepts - while maintaining model performance.","Unlike traditional approaches using post-hoc reconstruction (like Sparse Autoencoders), Monet integrates interpretability directly into its architecture. This enables both transparent understanding of model internals and fundamental behavior control. By scaling monosemantic experts, Monet paves the way for more transparent and controllable language models."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dmis-lab/Monet/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f302dfa038a88775b91c17ac10eb7a5b3583bd50bee9b54bc8bea6b9fbd529a7","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:29.020Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T04:52:29.020Z","projectInsights":{"version":